+      <summary>Sensor treated as CPU</summary>
+      <description>Substring identifying the CPU sensor on hardware the driver allow-list cannot recognise, matched against the hwmon chip name or thermal zone type. Upstream this defaults to empty; NCZ-OS sets "TZ" so the CIX Sky1 cluster zones (TZB0/TZB1/TZM0/TZM1) are read as CPU. The GPU hint is checked first, so TZGT is still classified as the GPU.</description>
+    </key>
+  
+    <!-- Keys added downstream 2026-08-14. The shell at upstream pin 995dd1e
+         reads these, but no schema in either repo defines them: upstream
+         singularity-shell ships only dev.sinty.lockscreen, so this file is the
+         sole definition site for dev.sinty.desktop. Tracking upstream tip
+         without adding them made singularity-desktop abort on startup:
+           GLib-GIO-ERROR: Settings schema 'dev.sinty.desktop' does not
+           contain a key named 'window-border-width'
+         GSettings treats a missing key as a programmer error and calls
+         g_error(), which aborts -- so every one of these is a hard crash the
+         moment its code path runs, not a fallback. Ranges below are taken from
+         the call sites, not invented. -->
+    <key name="window-border-width" type="i">
+      <default>1</default>
+      <range min="0" max="8"/>
+      <summary>Window border width</summary>
+      <description>
